    <h1>3 Cups of Coffee a Day: Why It Can Be Good for the Health</h1>
    <p class="muted">By John Goerke.</p>

    <p>Is 3 cups of coffee too much? Many people drink 3 cups of coffee a day, and 3 cups of black coffee a day is a common habit. This article looks at what that means, with moderation in mind.</p>

    <h2>Moderation</h2>
    <p>Like most things, coffee is best in moderation. How much is right varies from person to person, so 3 coffees a day may suit one person and be too much for another.</p>

    <h2>Caffeine</h2>
    <p>Caffeine is the main reason coffee is so widely enjoyed, and also the reason to pay attention to how much you drink. Your own sensitivity to caffeine matters when deciding whether 3 cups is too much.</p>

    <h2>Calories and what you add</h2>
    <p>Black coffee is low in calories. Sugar, syrups and cream are what raise the calorie count of a cup, so how you take your coffee matters as much as how many cups you drink.</p>

    <h2>Sleep</h2>
    <p>Caffeine late in the day can affect sleep. If coffee keeps you awake, try moving your cups earlier in the day.</p>

    <p>This article is general information, not medical advice; talk to a health professional about your own situation. Curious about nitro? Read <a href="/healthy-benefits-drinking-nitro-coffee-nitro-coffee-healthy/">the health benefits of drinking nitro coffee</a> or learn <a href="/nitro-cold-brew/">all about nitro cold brew</a>.</p>
